1
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Beyond darkness... beyond desolation... lies the greatest danger of all.

2
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug is a fantasy,
adventure, action film directed by Peter Jackson.

3
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
The Dwarves, Bilbo and Gandalf have successfully escaped the
Misty Mountains, and Bilbo has gained the One Ring.

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
They all continue their journey to get their gold back from the Dragon, Smaug.

5
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Gandalf the Grey, played by Ian McKellen.

6
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Bilbo Baggins, played by Martin Freeman.

7
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Thorin Oakenshield, played by Richard Armitage.

8
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Smaug / Sauron, played by Benedict Cumberbatch.

9
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Legolas, played by Orlando Bloom.

10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Tauriel, played by Evangeline Lilly.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug is a 2013 epic high fantasy adventure film directed by Peter Jackson from a screenplay
by Fran Walsh, Philippa Boyens, Jackson, and Guillermo del Toro, based on the 1937 novel The Hobbit by J.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The sequel to 2012's The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey, the film is the second instalment in The
Hobbit trilogy, acting as a prequel to Jackson's The Lord of the Rings trilogy.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
The film follows Bilbo Baggins as he continues to accompany Thorin Oakenshield and his
fellow dwarves on a quest to reclaim the Lonely Mountain from the dragon Smaug.

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
Pursuing them are the vengeful orcs Azog the Defiler and his son Bolg, while Gandalf the Grey
investigates the return of a long-forgotten evil force in the ruins of Dol Guldur.

15
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The ensemble cast includes Ian McKellen, Martin Freeman, Richard Armitage, Benedict Cumberbatch,
Evangeline Lilly, Lee Pace, Luke Evans, Ken Stott, James Nesbitt, and Orlando Bloom.

16
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The films were shot simultaneously in 3D at a projection rate of 48 frames per second, with
principal photography taking place around New Zealand and at Pinewood Studios.

17
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
Additional filming took place throughout May 2013.

18
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
The Desolation of Smaug premiered in Los Angeles on 2 December 2013, and was released
on 12 December in New Zealand and on 13 December in the United States.

19
02:13:00,000 --> 02:13:06,000
Produced by Warner Bros Pictures through its subsidiary New Line Cinema,  the film received mostly positive reviews and
grossed $959 million at the worldwide box office, making it the fourth highest-grossing film of 2013.

20
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
The film received numerous accolades; at the 86th Academy Awards, it was nominated
for Best Sound Editing, Best Sound Mixing, and Best Visual Effects.

21
02:27:00,000 --> 02:27:06,000
The final instalment of the trilogy, The Hobbit: The Battle
of the Five Armies, was released in 2014.

22
02:34:00,000 --> 02:34:06,000
The film explores themes of gold, lake, based on novel or book, elves, dwarf.
